DESCRIPTION Constraint band: a compound exclusion filter (literal plus prefix) plus a composite key format and sort.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "List the deployments in every namespace except kube-system and any namespace starting with kube-, one per line as namespace/deployment-name, sorted by namespace."
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 480 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

ASSERT(at least 1 specialist contributes with signal=agree)
ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)

# Deterministic, drift-tolerant ground truth: the cluster runs ~141 deployments across
# many namespaces. The question asks for ALL of them (one namespace/name per line), so a
# correct answer lists dozens of entries and the exclusion actually removes kube-system.
# The observed failure listed only 4. The numeric-bound count catches that gross
# under-report without pinning the exact total (>=40 holds even if the count drifts).
ASSERT(synthesis matches "[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*/[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*" at least 40 times)
ASSERT(synthesis does NOT CONTAIN "kube-system/")

# Reference-grounded quality: the deferred LLM judge (kubemoot-fitness crew) scores
# the synthesis against this ground truth on method and honesty, not specific values.
ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "The cluster runs many deployments across many namespaces, currently on the order of a hundred-plus outside the kube-* namespaces, so a correct answer is a long list, not a handful. It lists deployments from all namespaces while excluding kube-system and every kube-* namespace, formatted one per line as namespace/name and sorted by namespace, discovered live. Correct compound exclusion, format, sort, and completeness are scored; the specific deployment names are not. (The exact count drifts; the constant is enumerating every non-kube deployment in the required shape.)")
